WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.600
Welcome. You will decide whether the
receipt task needs a

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.200
model-directed loop, define its work
order, separate trusted authority from

3
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:16.800
proposals, inspect versioned transitions,
run all five terminal cases, modify

4
00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:22.400
a learner-owned input, and reconcile an
unknown outcome without a

5
00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:28.000
blind retry.

6
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:33.500
Start with the simplest design that can
meet the outcome.

7
00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:39.000
A fixed workflow for this receipt task can
validate the

8
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:44.500
input, check whether write_receipt is
allowed, check any required matching

9
00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:50.000
approval, preflight one action invocation,
write once, and independently verify

10
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:55.500
the receipt. Code owns every next step. A
model-directed loop

11
00:00:55.500 --> 00:01:01.000
becomes reasonable only when
representative observations contain

12
00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:06.500
necessary variation that makes the next
permitted action difficult to

13
00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:12.000
enumerate. Even then, the model proposes
rather than authorizes. The

14
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:17.500
offline fixture does not test model
reasoning and does not

15
00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:23.000
prove that agents outperform fixed
workflows. It tests whether the

16
00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:28.500
surrounding controller preserves
authority, budgets, state, evidence,

17
00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:34.000
terminals, and recovery.

18
00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:40.100
Read the completed work order. The outcome
is exactly one

19
00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:46.200
in-memory receipt containing APPROVED
colon prepare-agent-work and its operation

20
00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:52.300
key. Scope includes only the controller's
in-memory receipt array, state,

21
00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:58.400
trace, and bounded ledger. Trusted inputs
are the work order,

22
00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:04.500
policy, limits, verifier contract, initial
revision, and separate approval records.

23
00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:10.600
There is no network, credential,
paid-model, filesystem, or duplicate-write

24
00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:16.700
authority. Completion requires the
verifier to inspect the receipt text

25
00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:22.800
and operation key. Stop only at COMPLETE,
NEEDS_HUMAN, BUDGET_EXHAUSTED,

26
00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:28.900
POLICY_BLOCKED, or
FAILED_WITH_RECOVERY_EVIDENCE. This

27
00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:35.000
contract removes hidden decisions before
any proposal is evaluated.

28
00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:40.900
Observations and decisions are untrusted
data. They may request an

29
00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:46.800
action, but they cannot add it to policy,
increase a

30
00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:52.700
budget, choose a state revision, or
approve themselves. When approval

31
00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:58.600
is required, the separate trusted record
must exactly match action,

32
00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:04.500
resource, operationKey, and stateVersion.
A forged approvedByHuman field has no

33
00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:10.400
authority. Also distinguish policy from
approval. Policy answers whether an

34
00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:16.300
action is permitted at all. Approval
answers whether a particular

35
00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:22.200
permitted operation at a particular
revision has human authorization. The

36
00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:28.100
built-in success scenario requires no
approval. The changed practice scenario

37
00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:34.000
requires the existing matching trusted
approval.

38
00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:40.100
Represent the run as state rather than
conversation. One iteration

39
00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:46.200
inspects, decides, authorizes, preflights,
acts, verifies, and records. In the

40
00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:52.300
success fixture, beforeState has revision
one and no receipt. The

41
00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:58.400
decision proposes write_receipt with
expectedStateVersion one. Authorization

42
00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:04.500
checks the decision kind, implemented
action, policy, current revision, and

43
00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:10.600
any required approval. Preflight checks
the next fixture-time, fixture-token,

44
00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:16.700
turn, and action charges. The write
invocation is charged, creates

45
00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:22.800
one receipt, and advances revision to two.
Verification independently checks

46
00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:28.900
the receipt text and operation key. A
fluent finish proposal

47
00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:35.000
cannot replace that evidence.

48
00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:40.875
Budget accounting happens before the next
charge. maxActions counts every

49
00:04:40.875 --> 00:04:46.750
implemented act invocation, including a
noop or an unsuccessful attempt.

50
00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:52.625
It is not limited to successful or
consequential writes. A

51
00:04:52.625 --> 00:04:58.500
requested invocation that would move used
actions from zero to

52
00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:04.375
one is blocked when maxActions is zero.
Missing, negative, NaN,

53
00:05:04.375 --> 00:05:10.250
or Infinity costs are malformed and
produce POLICY_BLOCKED with zero

54
00:05:10.250 --> 00:05:16.125
effects. Fixture time and token cost are
deterministic accounting units,

55
00:05:16.125 --> 00:05:22.000
not measurements of wall-clock time or
provider tokens.

56
00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:27.600
Use exactly five lesson terminals.
COMPLETE means the independent

57
00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:33.200
postcondition passed. NEEDS_HUMAN follows
the third semantic no-progress transition.

58
00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:38.800
BUDGET_EXHAUSTED means a preflight charge
would exceed a configured limit.

59
00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:44.400
POLICY_BLOCKED means malformed or
unauthorized input was rejected before an

60
00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:50.000
effect. FAILED_WITH_RECOVERY_EVIDENCE
means a consequential invocation has an

61
00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:55.600
unknown outcome and may already have
changed the environment. These

62
00:05:55.600 --> 00:06:01.200
labels preserve causal evidence. Missing
policy is not a budget

63
00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:06.800
failure. A stale approval is not
no-progress. An unknown write

64
00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:12.400
result is not proof of failure and must
not be

65
00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:18.000
retried blindly.

66
00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:25.091
From the lab directory, run node --version
and confirm Node.js

67
00:06:25.091 --> 00:06:32.182
twenty-two or later. Run node --test and
inspect the report

68
00:06:32.182 --> 00:06:39.273
from your environment. The supplied
independent verification used version

69
00:06:39.273 --> 00:06:46.364
twenty-four point eighteen point zero and
