85
00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:46.600
Before editing, predict three variants.
What happens if you correct

86
00:08:46.600 --> 00:08:52.200
only policy? What happens if you correct
only maxActions? What

87
00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:57.800
happens if policy and budget are correct
but the required

88
00:08:57.800 --> 00:09:03.400
approval has the wrong stateVersion?
Record the terminal, effect count,

89
00:09:03.400 --> 00:09:09.000
and failed control for each.

90
00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:44.889
Correcting only policy lets authorization
proceed until the action preflight,

91
00:10:44.889 --> 00:10:50.778
where maxActions zero produces
BUDGET_EXHAUSTED before invocation.

92
00:10:50.778 --> 00:10:56.667
Correcting only maxActions does not grant
permission, so the result

93
00:10:56.667 --> 00:11:02.556
remains POLICY_BLOCKED with zero effects.
With policy and budget corrected,

94
00:11:02.556 --> 00:11:08.444
a stale required approval still produces
POLICY_BLOCKED with zero effects

95
00:11:08.444 --> 00:11:14.333
because stateVersion is part of the
approval binding. The same

96
00:11:14.333 --> 00:11:20.222
result applies to mismatched action,
resource, or operationKey. Separate checks

97
00:11:20.222 --> 00:11:26.111
make the cause visible and prevent one
trusted input from

98
00:11:26.111 --> 00:11:32.000
silently replacing another.

99
00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:37.667
Run node controller.js --scenario
uncertain --recover. The write fixture

100
00:11:37.667 --> 00:11:43.333
creates a receipt but reports an unknown
result. The original

101
00:11:43.333 --> 00:11:49.000
terminal remains
FAILED_WITH_RECOVERY_EVIDENCE. Recovery

102
00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:54.667
looks up the operation key before
considering a retry, finds

103
00:11:54.667 --> 00:12:00.333
one effect, and reports
retryPerformed=false. This avoids a

104
00:12:00.333 --> 00:12:06.000
duplicate write. The ledger is bounded to
thirty-two in-memory records

105
00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:11.667
and disappears when the process exits. It
is not durable

106
00:12:11.667 --> 00:12:17.333
idempotency, distributed concurrency
control, production security, or

107
00:12:17.333 --> 00:12:23.000
compliance evidence.

108
00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:29.000
Passing tests are necessary evidence, but
they can miss an

109
00:12:29.000 --> 00:12:35.000
authority flaw when the implementation and
tests share the same

110
00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:41.000
mistaken assumption. Independent checks
should rename scenarios so outcomes do

111
00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:47.000
not depend on fixture labels, mutate each
approval binding, test

112
00:12:47.000 --> 00:12:53.000
malformed and nonfinite costs, confirm
zero effects on pre-effect blocks,

113
00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:59.000
and verify that budgets remain bounded.
The supplied independent checks

114
00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:05.000
did those things for this fixture. They
still do not

115
00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:11.000
establish production adapter behavior,
model reasoning, persistent recovery,

116
00:13:11.000 --> 00:13:17.000
access control, or universal agent
superiority.

117
00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:22.333
Begin the lab. Retain your test report,
exact five-line summary,

118
00:13:22.333 --> 00:13:27.667
success trace, learner-owned changed
input, changed result, three-variant

119
00:13:27.667 --> 00:13:33.000
diagnosis, and uncertain recovery result.
For every case, identify state

120
00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:38.333
before and after, the first failed or
successful controller check,

121
00:13:38.333 --> 00:13:43.667
the effect count, budget use, terminal
reason, and evidence supporting

122
00:13:43.667 --> 00:13:49.000
that terminal.

123
00:33:49.000 --> 00:33:56.000
Debrief your results. The built-in success
trace reaches COMPLETE without

124
00:33:56.000 --> 00:34:03.000
a human approval requirement. The
unchanged practice input is POLICY_BLOCKED

125
00:34:03.000 --> 00:34:10.000
because policy omits write_receipt. The
changed practice input reaches COMPLETE

126
00:34:10.000 --> 00:34:17.000
only after policy permits the action and
maxActions permits one

127
00:34:17.000 --> 00:34:24.000
invocation, while its existing required
approval remains an exact match.

128
00:34:24.000 --> 00:34:31.000
Three rejected finish proposals lead to
NEEDS_HUMAN. A preflight overspend

129
00:34:31.000 --> 00:34:38.000
leads to BUDGET_EXHAUSTED. Malformed or
unauthorized input leads to

130
00:34:38.000 --> 00:34:45.000
POLICY_BLOCKED. The uncertain write
preserves FAILED_WITH_RECOVERY_EVIDENCE,

131
00:34:45.000 --> 00:34:52.000
